      "problem": "Evaluate ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{4}{-(n+1)}^{2}.$",
      "worked_solution": "The sum takes integer values of $n$ from $1$ to $4.$ So, computing the terms for $n=1,2,3,4$ and then adding them, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{4}{-(n+1)}^{2} & =(-(1+1)^{2})+(-(2+1)^{2})+(-(3+1)^{2})+(-(4+1)^{2}) \\\\  & =-(2)^{2}-(3)^{2}-(4)^{2}-(5)^{2} \\\\  & =-4-9-16-25 \\\\  & =-54.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
